!!! THIRD PASS — 2026-08-06, the seat stops reading a private label

''A reading of the rite against the identity plane found the movement-② join reaching for the wrong
name.'' The seal matched each chair against the operator's ''PRIVATE pet-name'', which welded two
registers the plane holds apart: an operator could seat only under the string they call the compartment
at home, so every private label became a public commitment by construction, and a compartment called
`the-burner` could never stand as `The Lindwyrm`.

''Nothing had leaked'' — the published string always came from the seal's own seed — so the finding names
a ''forced coupling'', never a disclosure. The correction gives the outward intent its own store and its
own act (`--handle`), and the chair claim a third (`--seat`), and re-points the join at the declared
Handle. Movement ② carries the new sequence; ⊛ gather gains `persona sync`, because both names now ride
the human's own fleet.

''What a rehearsal watches here.'' That the two registers stay ''visibly different'' — set a private
label that reads nothing like the chair name and confirm the seat still lands. A rehearsal that types the
same string into both flags proves nothing, because a label-matching join would pass it too.

''AND THE SAME READING FOUND TWO MORE, both un-pono for the same reason'' (operator, 2026-08-07):

# ''THE FOUNDING NAMES SHIPPED IN THE BUILD.'' A `FOUNDING_KAHU` constant carried three display names, so
  the SOURCE decided who the founding kahu were and the operator merely confirmed it. ''Retired.'' The
  scaffold now names nobody, and the roster forms at the seat from the personas that declared and stood.
  The threshold followed the same cut: a `2` written into a file would seat one Nexus's fairness call inside
