''A name that inverts its own meaning beside a destructive command is a trap, not a label.''

''RULED'': the pet-name goes. ''OPEN'': what replaces it — a coinage against a living lexicon's own technical
decision belongs in a talk-story, never in a unilateral swap, and `hoʻomaka` stands unchecked for the same
collision. ''The concept keeps its grounding'' (Direct Boot BFU/AFU · SPIRE · kubelet TLS bootstrap ·
Tang/Clevis) and its meme; only the handle falls.
